# Members whose value #2022's gate cannot show travels in the state blob.
#
# Read by src/doppler/tests/test_mutator_state.py: every public member of
# every serializable class, as Python gets it, and every C setter the class
# does not bind, probed by behaviour. A member that does not pass (TRAVELS,
# KEYED or READS) must be listed here once, with EXACTLY the verdict it reads
# and a reason, or the gate is red. A listed member that now passes, names
# nothing, or reads another verdict is red too, and `make tests-ssot` refuses
# a key the merge base did not hold: this list only shrinks. The rule is
# docs/design/state-serialization.md, "What goes in the blob".
#
#   LOST              its value does not travel: a fix deletes the line
#   NONDETERMINISTIC  two identical builds differ, so no restore can be judged
#   UNPROBED          the probe cannot show it either way (reason: why)
#   CRASHES           its probe kills the process, so a child confirms it
#   C_ONLY            no Python face to probe: verified by a C twin, #2077
#   NO_RECIPE         its class has no CASES row to probe with, #2078
#
# Each family's fix PR deletes its own lines (#2079..#2084, LO/NCO first).
#
# key                                                   verdict           reason

# -- LOST (17)
